  "issue": {
    "headline": "A city that publishes a lot, and what still is not in it",
    "body": "Austin is unusually good at publishing — eDIMS, an open-data portal, a full Legistar instance, a televised archive going back decades. That makes it the right place to ask the harder question: with all of that published, which categories of record still require a request, and what do the AG rulings say the City asked to withhold anyway.",
    "record": "Attorney General open-records rulings naming the City of Austin, read against what eDIMS already publishes."
  },
